31702385646592,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":75.2,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.42063757178256583,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":29.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.21138525187415047,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":87.1,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.03026127068264555,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":23.2,"_gate_pool_share":0.01093669306154399,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":44.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.02850094455953056,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.004141836410619115,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":45.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.13451207398863885,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.12395656818342204,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0016828680414311254,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.01507,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.778,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":77.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"AutoNation, Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates as an automotive retailer in the United States. The company operates through four segments: Domestic, Import, Premium Luxury, and AutoNation Finance. It offers a range of automotive products and services, including new and used vehicles; and parts and services, such as automotive repair and maintenance, and wholesale parts and collision services. The company also provides automotive finance and insurance products comprising vehicle services and other protection products; and indirect financing, as well as arranges finance for vehicle purchases through third-party finance sources. It owns and operates new vehicle franchises from stores located in metropolitan markets in the Sunbelt region, as well as AutoNation-branded collision centers, AutoNation USA used vehicle stores, AutoNation-branded automotive auction operations, and parts distribution centers. The company was formerly known as Republic Industries, Inc. and changed its name to AutoNation, Inc. in 1999. AutoNation, Inc. was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Fort Lauderdale, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael M. Manley | CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 24K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["AutoNation, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $5.9B market cap on $27.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $198M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.9\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 13.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Insiders are net buyers (78% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Driving AutoNation\u2019s (NYSE:AN) Changing Business Mix?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/what-is-driving-autonations-nysean-cha