ine, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.8% over 3 years, 6.3% over 5 years and 2.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00, a backlog worth 0% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 3%.","Capex runs 1.8x depreciation (1.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.5%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $722K bought.","It returns 13.5% a year to shareholders (13.5% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 12.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 14.5% of the float, 4.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 24,800 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, 2.9x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 5.5% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$8K per employee.","CEO pay is $6.3M (6x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":72,"head":"Invest: trades 57% below fair value of $423; ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 7.0%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 46, gates 13/25)","Trades 57% below fair value of $423","ROIC 22.0% vs WACC 7.0%","Altman Z in the safe zone","P/E 8.8x vs sector 19.3x"],"cons":["FCF margin 0.7% (burns cash)","Net debt/EBITDA 3.1x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":359.92,"vc":{"base":423.44,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":423.44,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.5733,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (57% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"AN","date":"2026-11-06"}